.TH nl 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
nl \- number lines of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY nl
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ FILE \~.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Write each FILE to standard output, with line numbers added.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-b
\fB\-b, \-\-body\-numbering=\,STYLE\fP
.UE
use STYLE for numbering body lines
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-d
\fB\-d, \-\-section\-delimiter=\,CC\fP
.UE
use CC for logical page delimiters
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-f
\fB\-f, \-\-footer\-numbering=\,STYLE\fP
.UE
use STYLE for numbering footer lines
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-h
\fB\-h, \-\-header\-numbering=\,STYLE\fP
.UE
use STYLE for numbering header lines
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-i
\fB\-i, \-\-line\-increment=\,NUMBER\fP
.UE
line number increment at each line
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-l
\fB\-l, \-\-join\-blank\-lines=\,NUMBER\fP
.UE
group of NUMBER empty lines counted as one
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-n
\fB\-n, \-\-number\-format=\,FORMAT\fP
.UE
insert line numbers according to FORMAT
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-p
\fB\-p, \-\-no\-renumber\fP
.UE
do not reset line numbers for each section
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-s
\fB\-s, \-\-number\-separator=\,STRING\fP
.UE
add STRING after (possible) line number
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-v
\fB\-v, \-\-starting\-line\-number=\,NUMBER\fP
.UE
first line number for each section
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#nl\-w
\fB\-w, \-\-number\-width=\,NUMBER\fP
.UE
use NUMBER columns for line numbers
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/nl#nl\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/nl#nl\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
.PP
Default options are: \fB\-bt\fR \fB\-d\fR'\e:' \fB\-fn\fR \fB\-hn\fR \fB\-i1\fR \fB\-l1\fR \fB\-n\fR'rn' \fB\-s\fR<TAB> \fB\-v1\fR \fB\-w6\fR
.PP
CC are two delimiter characters used to construct logical page delimiters;
a missing second character implies ':'.  As a GNU extension one can specify
more than two characters, and also specifying the empty string (\fB\-d\fR '')
disables section matching.
.PP
STYLE is one of:
.TP
a
number all lines
.TP
t
number only nonempty lines
.TP
n
number no lines
.TP
pBRE
number only lines that contain a match for the basic regular
expression, BRE
.PP
FORMAT is one of:
.TP
ln
left justified, no leading zeros
.TP
rn
right justified, no leading zeros
.TP
rz
right justified, leading zeros
